<title>COLOMBIA: Mexico and Colombia target higher coffee output.</title>
<headline>Mexico and Colombia target higher coffee output.</headline>
<dateline>ARMENIA, Colombia 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico plans to boost its annual coffee out to a total of about 8 million 60-kg bags by 2000 from a current output of 4.7 million bags, said Ruben Castillo, executive president of the Mexican Coffee Council.</p>
<p>Castillo spoke of the ambitious plan to nearly double Mexico's coffee production within three years at a meeting Friday partly sponsored by National Coffee Growers' Federation in this city in the heart of Colombia's central coffee-growing region.</p>
</text>
